course: dictionary
lesson: 13318
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. The clues in the sentence show you which meaning the writer wants. Grooming is one of these words. «The monkeys spent the afternoon grooming each other.» Monkeys and each other tell you grooming means cleaning and brushing fur.
explain: Grooming can also mean keeping yourself clean and tidy, or getting someone ready for a job or role. «Mum took the dog to the groomer for a bath and a trim.» Here the dog is the clue, so grooming means cleaning and brushing an animal's coat. Always check the clues, then try your meaning in the sentence.
explain: One meaning is a serious warning sign. Sometimes an adult or older person tricks a child into trusting them so they can harm them. This is called grooming. «If an online friend asks you to keep secrets from your parents, that is a warning sign.» If anything like this happens to you, tell a trusted adult straight away. You will not be in trouble for telling.
fact: Grooming means cleaning, brushing or tidying something, such as an animal's fur or your own hair.
fact: «Personal grooming» means keeping yourself clean and tidy: washing, combing your hair and cutting your nails.
fact: Grooming can mean getting someone ready for a job or role, as in «She was grooming her deputy to take over the team.»
fact: When grooming means an adult tricking a child to harm them, it is a danger. Warning signs include secrets, gifts, and requests to meet alone.
fact: If you see a warning sign, tell a trusted adult, such as a parent, carer or teacher, straight away.
exercise: «The cat spent a long time grooming its fur after dinner.» What does grooming mean here? | *Cleaning and brushing its coat | Hiding from the dog | Chasing a mouse
exercise: «She was grooming her younger sister to take over the team captain role.» What does grooming mean here? | Hurting someone | Telling a secret | *Getting someone ready for a role | Cleaning her sister's fur
exercise: «Brushing your teeth and combing your hair are part of personal grooming.» What is personal grooming? | Cleaning out a bedroom | *Keeping yourself clean and tidy | Brushing an animal | Playing a game
test: «Tom spent Saturday grooming the horse before the show.» Which meaning fits? | Keeping his bedroom tidy | Winning a race | Telling a secret | *Cleaning and brushing the horse's coat
test: «An adult asks you to keep a secret from your family.» What should you do? | Meet them alone | Keep the secret because they are nice | *Tell a trusted adult straight away | Promise never to tell anyone
exam: «The new coach spent the term grooming young players for the national team.» What does grooming mean here? | *Getting them ready for a role | Brushing their hair | Cleaning their boots
